description: Festive Week 1-2 queue is New publish only — never Optimize existing posts.
alwaysApply: true
---

# New blogs only (ignore Optimize)

For BlueStone festive SEO articles from `SEO Strategy 2026.xlsx` → `Week 1-2`:

1. **Always publish a new WordPress post** (new slug, `publish_*` flow).
2. **Ignore** sheet `Action = Optimize`. Do not patch or rewrite an existing BlueStone URL for that keyword.
3. If the sheet still shows an old BlueStone Blog URL on an Optimize-turned-New row, treat it as **reference only** — do not update that post. Create a fresh URL instead.
4. Do **not** invent a second post for ranks already completed (see Execution Note / live URL). Completed historical Optimize rows stay as-is; do not redo them as New unless the user asks.
5. Template script: `scripts/publish_diwali_article.py` / `publish_bhai_dooj_article.py`. Do not start from `optimize_*.py` for new queue work.
---
description: Mid-article product carousels must use ProductImages/seo images only (never raw packshots).
alwaysApply: true
---

# Carousel images = SEO images only

When building or patching BlueStone festive blog carousels (`bs-cf`):

1. **Source Type 2 carousel cards only from** `ProductImages/seo images/<Category>/<Exact Product Name>.png`.
2. **Never** use `ProductImages/raw/`, multi-angle folders, CDN `giproduct` primary packshots, or Google feed images for carousel cards.
3. Convert those SEO PNGs to WebP (~960×535, quality ~82) before upload; filename `{product-slug}-carousel.webp`.
4. Carousel alt: `{occasion/KW + year} gift idea: {Exact Product Name}`; set WP media `title` + `alt_text` on upload (see `.cursor/rules/image-seo.mdc`).
5. Raw / CDN product angles are for **Type 3 Higgsfield prompts only** (`reference_images` → MCP `media_import_url`), not the mid-article carousel.
6. If an SEO image is missing for an approved SKU, stop and ask — do not fall back to raw.

This applies to all New article scripts (`publish_*`) and any live carousel image swaps. (Legacy `optimize_*` scripts are not used for new queue work.)
# Type 3 casting: fair-skinned Indians only

When generating BlueStone festive blog Type 3 images (hero, lifestyle, or any scene with visible people/skin):

1. **Cast fair-skinned Indian subjects only** — light wheatish to fair North Indian / urban Indian complexion.
2. State casting explicitly in the prompt (e.g. "fair-skinned Indian father and child").
3. Add negatives: `dark skin, deep brown skin, heavily tanned skin`.
4. Applies to faces, hands, wrists, necks — any visible skin.
5. Flatlay with **no people** is exempt.
6. Do not regenerate or ship people images that default to deep/dark complexions when the brief calls for Indian lifestyle.

This applies to Higgsfield MCP (current Type 3 provider) and any future Type 3 generator.
---
description: Image SEO for BlueStone festive blogs: filenames, alts, media titles, WebP.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Image SEO (Type 2 + Type 3)

For every festive blog publish:

1. **WebP only** for carousel and Type 3 (q ~82). No heavy PNG heroes.
2. **Filenames:** Type 3 `{occasion}-{hero|flatlay|lifestyle}-{year}.webp`; Type 2 `{product-slug}-carousel.webp`.
3. **Alts unique** with locked festive year + product/scene. **Primary KW in hero alt.**
4. **Carousel alts:** `{occasion/KW + year} gift idea: {Exact Product Name}` (not bare product name).
5. **WP media titles** descriptive on upload (`alt_text` + `title` together). Sync body `wp:image` alts.
5b. **Type 3 body captions:** flatlay + lifestyle Gutenberg images need a short editorial `<figcaption>` that names the product and naturally reflects the target keyword/intent. Avoid robotic patterns like `detail: Product`, `look: Product`, or `vibe: Product`. Rotate products across articles (see `product-rotation-captions-education.mdc`).
6. Featured hero must **not** also appear in the body.
7. Gutenberg Type 3: `sizeSlug: "full"` only. No `large` + `width`/`height`/`loading`/`decoding`.

Canonical detail: `KnowledgeBase/Writing/HIGGSFIELD_IMAGE_GENERATION.md` → **Image SEO**.

Type 3 people heroes: use people-first prompts + 2 product refs max (see HIGGSFIELD_IMAGE_GENERATION.md). Macro/commercial jewellery lead-ins cause floating packshot overlays.

Credits: exactly **3** Type 3 images per article (`count: 1` each for hero/flatlay/lifestyle). Retry a slot only if QA fails. No dual variants by default. **Campaign hybrid:** candid people + HD jewellery. Lifestyle/hero refs: `@img1` body_image + `@img2` design. Short scale line: keep size like `@img1` body_image; `@img2` design only; do not make bigger for visibility. **If body_image missing, skip that SKU** (do not generate people shots from packshots only). **Flatlay:** rotate setting ID from 8-menu; log in `product_rotation.json`. See HIGGSFIELD_IMAGE_GENERATION.md.

Avoid empty-screen visuals: do not include visible phones, laptops, tablets, TVs, or blank screens in Type 3 prompts. Use physical props instead. If a device must be present, show only the edge/back or angle the screen away/out of frame. Never prompt for readable text on screens.
