+# Week 6 Rank 3 structure and visual concept
+
+## Article brief
+
+- Engine: buying_guide
+- Content mode: education
+- Title A: Bangle Size Chart 2026: How to Measure the Right Fit
+- Title B for later same-URL CTR testing: Bangle Size Guide 2026: Chart, Measurements and Fit Tips
+- Slug: bangle-size-2026
+- Meta title: Bangle Size Chart 2026 and Measurement Guide
+- Meta description: Find your bangle size with an Indian size chart in mm, cm and inches. Learn two accurate measuring methods, fit checks and buying tips.
+- Author: Vikas, WordPress user 270271338
+- Categories: Jewellery Problem & Solution 554493465; Bangle 554493412
+- Target visible length: 2,400 to 3,000 words
+- Commerce approach: one useful mid-article carousel with six approved bangle examples. No price language and no gift framing.
+
+## Ordered structure
+
+1. Direct answer and TL;DR
+2. Bangle size chart in mm, cm and inches
+3. How to measure bangle size using a bangle you own
+4. How to measure your hand for bangle size at home
+5. Closed, openable and adjustable bangle sizing explained
+6. Bangle designs to compare before choosing a size, with six-product carousel
+7. How should a correctly sized bangle fit?
+8. Common bangle size mistakes and how to fix them
+9. Choosing a size for wide, oval and stackable bangles
+10. Bangle size buying checklist for online orders
+11. When to visit a BlueStone store for a fitting
+12. More bangle guides
+13. Conclusion
+14. Frequently asked questions about bangle size
+15. Fact sources
+
+## Product carousel
+
+All carousel assets exist in `ProductImages/seo images/Bangles/` and all products are approved in `Seo Products - final products (1).csv`.
+
+1. BENS0325O09, The Tarentella Oval Bangle
+2. BISM0003O14, The Muricelle Bangle
+3. BIPS0003O06, The Channing Bangle
+4. BIDG0393O37, The Estrella Oval Bangle
+5. BINK0363B03, The Skein Bangle
+6. BISL0804O13, The Pear Evil Eye Toggle Bangle
+
+The carousel illustrates why shape, hinge construction, width, and profile should be checked after converting a hand measurement. It is not presented as a sizing guarantee.
+
+## Type 3 visual concept
+
+Model: nano_banana_pro, 16:9, 2k, one result per slot.
+
+Flatlay setting: `desk-kraft`. Week 6 Rank 2 used `study-desk`, so this does not repeat the consecutive setting. The desk scene will omit cards and readable objects.
+
+### Hero
+
+- Product: BIDG0393O37, The Estrella Oval Bangle
+- Body image gate: passed, `ProductImages/raw/Bangles/The Estrella Oval Bangle/1_body_portrait.png`
+- Design reference: `ProductImages/raw/Bangles/The Estrella Oval Bangle/0_primary.png`
+- Scene: fair-skinned Indian adult woman at a clean jewellery counter, fingers grouped as if slipping on a bangle while a jeweller uses an unmarked cloth tape around the widest part of her hand. The Estrella bangle is physically worn at true scale on the other wrist.
+- Intent: a clear educational measurement moment, not a romantic or gift scene.
+
+### Flatlay
+
+- Product: BIPS0003O06, The Channing Bangle
+- References: primary, front, side and close-up packshots
+- Scene: top-down desk-kraft flatlay with the bangle at true scale, a plain cloth measuring tape without legible numbers, a metal ruler turned so marks are soft and unreadable, a circular bangle sizing cone, and folded cream fabric.
+- Caption: The Channing Bangle beside simple tools used to confirm bangle size and inner diameter
+
+### Lifestyle
+
+- Product: BINK0363B03, The Skein Bangle
+- Body image gate: passed, `ProductImages/raw/Bangles/The Skein Bangle/1_body_portrait.png`
+- Design reference: `ProductImages/raw/Bangles/The Skein Bangle/0_primary.png`
+- Scene: fair-skinned Indian adult woman at a jewellery counter sliding the bangle over grouped fingers while a jeweller guides the hand. The bangle is physically on the hand, with the full face, wrist and fingers in frame.
+- Caption: The Skein Bangle being checked over the widest part of the hand for a comfortable fit
+
+## Visual restrictions
+
+- People shots use exactly two references: body image first, design image second.
+- Female products appear only on adult women.
+- Product dimensions are described as jewellery dimensions, never face or body measurements.
+- No phones, screens, certificates, invoices, cards, boards, placards, logos, or readable text.
+- No floating product overlays, extra jewellery, enlarged jewellery, cropped heads, cropped hands, or distorted fingers.
+- Required filmic language appears in all three prompts.
+- Featured hero is not repeated in the body.
+
+## Differentiation from existing BlueStone article
+
+Post 14544 already explains basic at-home measurement. This new article will lead with the full conversion chart, distinguish closed from openable construction, diagnose fit, explain wide and oval forms, add a purchase checklist, and show decision points for professional fitting. The older article will be linked as a shorter companion rather than duplicated sentence by sentence.
