+  "more_reads_html": "Use the shorter guide to <a href=\"https://blog.bluestone.com/how-to-measure-bangle-size-at-home-accurately/\">measure bangle size at home</a>, compare <a href=\"https://blog.bluestone.com/the-fit-test-every-bangle-should-pass-before-you-buy-it/\">the fit test every bangle should pass</a>, learn <a href=\"https://blog.bluestone.com/what-is-the-difference-between-a-bangle-and-a-bracelet-complete-guide/\">the difference between a bangle and a bracelet</a>, or explore <a href=\"https://blog.bluestone.com/gold-bangles-design-2026/\">gold bangle designs for 2026</a>.",
+  "tail_h2": "How to use this bangle size guide before buying",
+  "how_to_html": "Write down three things before you shop: the measurement, the method used, and the bangle construction you plan to buy. Compare all three with the exact product page. If the values disagree, you are between sizes, or the design is wide or oval, pause the order and ask for a professional fitting.",
+  "faq_h2": "Frequently Asked Questions about Bangle Size",
+  "section_leads": {
+    "Bangle size chart in mm, cm and inches": "The <a href=\"https://climg6.bluestone.com/static/resources/themes/bluestone/docs/Bangle_Measuring_Guide.pdf\">BlueStone Bangle Measuring Guide</a> and the Gem and Jewellery Skill Council of India retail training handbook use the standard inner-diameter progression below. Values are rounded for practical measuring, so retain millimetres until you have chosen the closest size.",
+    "How to measure bangle size using a bangle you own": "This is usually the simplest method because it copies a fit that already works. Accuracy depends on choosing a comfortable, undistorted reference and measuring only the clear opening through its true centre.",
+    "How to measure your hand for bangle size at home": "Use the hand method when you do not own a suitable reference bangle. The measurement must represent the widest shape the closed bangle will pass over, not the narrower wrist where it eventually rests.",
+    "Closed, openable and adjustable bangle sizing explained": "Bangle construction changes the fitting route. Closed designs slide over the hand, while hinged and adjustable designs can open closer to the wrist. Match the method to the mechanism before converting a number.",
+    "How should a correctly sized bangle fit?": "The correct fit is secure and wearable, not merely possible to put on. Check the entire sequence from passing the hand to moving at the wrist and removing the bangle again.",
+    "Common bangle size mistakes and how to fix them": "Most wrong-size orders begin with a small measurement error or the wrong reference point. A second reading and a construction check can prevent a centimetre, diameter, or wrist measurement from being applied to the wrong product.",
+    "Choosing a size for wide, oval and stackable bangles": "A size label cannot describe every contact point. Width, profile, internal shape, hinges, stones, and neighbouring bangles all change how a design feels during wear.",
